<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiongnu Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Xiongnu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xiongnu Empire was a confederation of nomadic peoples that dominated the eastern Eurasian steppe from the late third century BCE to the first century CE. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modu-chanyu">Modu</a> it united the steppe tribes and became a strong rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>, extracting tribute through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heqin">heqin</a> system. Weakened by Han campaigns and internal division, it fragmented, though its political model influenced later steppe empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire.jpg" alt="Xiongnu Empire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gary Todd · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Warring_States_Xiongnu_Gold_Crown_-_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Han military combined a conscript infantry base with a professional cavalry arm developed specifically to counter the <b>Xiongnu</b> nomadic confederation, the empire's most persistent strategic threat.</blockquote><a href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Since the 18th century historians have debated a link with the <b>Xiongnu</b> of Mongolia, and there is no consensus.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hunnic-empire">Hunnic Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Kushans were one of five branches of the Yuezhi, a people driven from the Gansu corridor by the <b>Xiongnu</b> in the 2nd century BCE, who settled in Bactria, north of the Hindu Kush, by about 130 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kushan-empire">Kushan Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Jin dynasty allied with them against the <b>Xiongnu</b> state of Han-Zhao, and in 315 the chief Tuoba Yilu was made Prince of Dai; Dai stagnated after him and fell to Former Qin in 376.</blockquote><a href="/empire/northern-wei">Northern Wei · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 215 BCE the general Meng Tian conquered the Ordos from the <b>Xiongnu</b>, who had raided Qin peasants forbidden to trade with them.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Saka world of the steppe was broken by migrations set off by the rise of the <b>Xiongnu</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/saka">Saka · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
